WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.650 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Imagine you are waiting for a bus.

2
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:07.410 line:1% position:50% size:90%
It leaves at nine fifteen and reaches your
destination at ten oh five.

3
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:11.720 line:1% position:50% size:90%
You glance at the clock and wonder, how
long did the journey really take?

4
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.410 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Could it be ten minutes?

5
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.980 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Or is there something we are missing?

6
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.870 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Let us find out together.

7
00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:23.195 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Today we are learning how to read time and
calculate duration.

8
00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:27.245 line:1% position:50% size:90%
By the end, you will be able to solve our
bus mystery yourself.

9
00:00:28.253 --> 00:00:32.543 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Our learning goal is to read time
accurately, calculate elapsed time, and

10
00:00:32.543 --> 00:00:35.513 line:1% position:50% size:90%
explain our thinking using clocks and
timelines.

11
00:00:36.515 --> 00:00:41.225 line:1% position:50% size:90%
By the end, you can read the hour and
minute hands, calculate a duration

12
00:00:41.225 --> 00:00:44.575 line:1% position:50% size:90%
that crosses the hour, and check your
answer with a timeline.

13
00:00:45.588 --> 00:00:47.458 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Start with the minute hand.

14
00:00:47.468 --> 00:00:50.798 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Each large step around the clock is five
minutes.

15
00:00:50.818 --> 00:00:54.588 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The minute hand at three means fifteen
minutes past the hour.

16
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:57.897 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Now find the short hour hand.

17
00:00:57.937 --> 00:01:02.157 line:1% position:50% size:90%
It sits a little after nine, because
fifteen minutes of the ninth hour have

18
00:01:02.157 --> 00:01:05.187 line:1% position:50% size:90%
passed. This clock shows nine fifteen.

19
00:01:06.202 --> 00:01:07.632 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Look at this clock.

20
00:01:07.672 --> 00:01:09.422 line:1% position:50% size:90%
What time does it show?

21
00:01:09.452 --> 00:01:12.562 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Read the minute hand first, then the hour
hand.

22
00:01:12.592 --> 00:01:15.392 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Give yourself five seconds to decide.

23
00:01:20.395 --> 00:01:23.805 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The minute hand points to eight, or forty
minutes.

24
00:01:23.845 --> 00:01:26.745 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The hour hand is between three and four.

25
00:01:26.796 --> 00:01:29.646 line:1% position:50% size:90%
It is three forty, not eight fifteen.

26
00:01:30.669 --> 00:01:32.879 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Let's return to our bus journey.

27
00:01:32.879 --> 00:01:36.719 line:1% position:50% size:90%
It begins at nine fifteen and finishes at
ten oh five.

28
00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:40.769 line:1% position:50% size:90%
We can make the calculation easier by
jumping to the next hour.

29
00:01:41.816 --> 00:01:45.546 line:1% position:50% size:90%
From nine fifteen to ten o'clock, how many
minutes pass?

30
00:01:45.556 --> 00:01:49.486 line:1% position:50% size:90%
You could count in fives, or subtract
fifteen from sixty.

31
00:01:54.506 --> 00:01:58.586 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Forty-five minutes pass between nine
fifteen and ten o'clock.

32
00:01:58.596 --> 00:02:01.046 line:1% position:50% size:90%
That is our first part of the journey.

33
00:02:02.046 --> 00:02:06.976 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Then the bus travels another five minutes,
from ten o'clock to ten oh five.

34
00:02:06.996 --> 00:02:08.426 line:1% position:50% size:90%
We add the two parts:

35
00:02:08.426 --> 00:02:11.296 line:1% position:50% size:90%
forty-five plus five equals fifty minutes.

36
00:02:12.312 --> 00:02:16.942 line:1% position:50% size:90%
A common mistake is to subtract fifteen
from five and say the journey took

37
00:02:16.942 --> 00:02:20.322 line:1% position:50% size:90%
ten minutes. That ignores the change of
hour.

38
00:02:20.342 --> 00:02:23.172 line:1% position:50% size:90%
A timeline makes the missing minutes
visible.

39
00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.030 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Now let's read twenty-four-hour time.

40
00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:31.140 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Nine fifteen in the morning is written
zero nine fifteen.

41
00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:34.860 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Three forty in the afternoon is written
fifteen forty.

42
00:02:35.849 --> 00:02:39.559 line:1% position:50% size:90%
For afternoon times after twelve, add
twelve to the hour.

43
00:02:39.589 --> 00:02:42.029 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Three plus twelve equals fifteen.

44
00:02:42.059 --> 00:02:44.009 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The minutes do not change.

45
00:02:45.035 --> 00:02:49.185 line:1% position:50% size:90%
A movie begins at thirteen twenty and ends
at fourteen ten.

46
00:02:49.215 --> 00:02:51.595 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Before I reveal the answer, estimate:

47
00:02:51.595 --> 00:02:55.195 line:1% position:50% size:90%
is the duration closer to thirty minutes
or one hour?

48
00:03:00.261 --> 00:03:04.191 line:1% position:50% size:90%
From thirteen twenty to fourteen hundred
is forty minutes.

49
00:03:04.211 --> 00:03:07.331 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Another ten minutes takes us to fourteen
ten.

50
00:03:07.381 --> 00:03:09.501 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The total is fifty minutes.

51
00:03:10.309 --> 00:03:12.599 line:1% position:50% size:90%
We can also use the word quarter.

52
00:03:12.639 --> 00:03:15.699 line:1% position:50% size:90%
A quarter of sixty minutes is fifteen
minutes.

53
00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:19.479 line:1% position:50% size:90%
When the minute hand points to three, it
is quarter past the hour.

54
00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:22.629 line:1% position:50% size:90%
When it points to nine, it is quarter to
the next hour.

55
00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:26.224 line:1% position:50% size:90%
This clock shows nine forty-five.

56
00:03:26.264 --> 00:03:29.364 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Is that quarter past nine, or quarter to
ten?

57
00:03:29.404 --> 00:03:32.974 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Look closely at where the shorter hour
hand is moving.

58
00:03:33.004 --> 00:03:35.794 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Give yourself five seconds to decide.

59
00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.530 line:1% position:50% size:90%
It is quarter to ten.

60
00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.580 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Forty-five minutes have already passed
since nine o'clock, and fifteen

61
00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.340 line:1% position:50% size:90%
minutes remain until ten.

62
00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.920 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The hour hand is nearly at ten.

63
00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:53.480 line:1% position:50% size:90%
That is why we say quarter to ten.

64
00:03:54.318 --> 00:03:57.738 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Think of ten o'clock as a friendly
stopping point.

65
00:03:57.748 --> 00:04:01.028 line:1% position:50% size:90%
First travel from nine fifteen to ten
o'clock.

66
00:04:01.028 --> 00:04:04.278 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Then travel from ten o'clock to ten oh
five.

67
00:04:04.298 --> 00:04:08.528 line:1% position:50% size:90%
We can add the two durations because the
parts do not overlap.

68
00:04:09.565 --> 00:04:14.265 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Try another example. A swimming lesson
begins at two twenty-five

69
00:04:14.265 --> 00:04:15.965 line:1% position:50% size:90%
and finishes at three ten.

70
00:04:15.985 --> 00:04:18.675 line:1% position:50% size:90%
How many minutes until three o'clock?

71
00:04:18.735 --> 00:04:21.635 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Then how many more minutes until three
ten?

72
00:04:21.665 --> 00:04:24.125 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Work it out before the explanation.

73
00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:33.313 line:1% position:50% size:90%
From two twenty-five to three o'clock is
thirty-five minutes.

74
00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:37.063 line:1% position:50% size:90%
From three o'clock to three ten is another
ten minutes.

75
00:04:37.073 --> 00:04:40.733 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Thirty-five plus ten equals forty-five
minutes.

76
00:04:40.763 --> 00:04:43.913 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The swimming lesson lasts forty-five
minutes.

77
00:04:44.935 --> 00:04:47.585 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Check the reasonableness of your answer.

78
00:04:47.645 --> 00:04:52.095 line:1% position:50% size:90%
If an activity begins before three o'clock
and finishes just after three

79
00:04:52.095 --> 00:04:55.465 line:1% position:50% size:90%
o'clock, a duration of five minutes is too
short.

80
00:04:55.475 --> 00:04:58.995 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Estimate first, then calculate to catch
mistakes.

81
00:04:59.808 --> 00:05:01.478 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Here is a quick check.

82
00:05:01.498 --> 00:05:05.718 line:1% position:50% size:90%
If a sports match starts at fourteen
twenty, what time is that on a twelve-

83
00:05:05.718 --> 00:05:09.588 line:1% position:50% size:90%
hour clock? Think about subtracting twelve
from the hour.

84
00:05:09.588 --> 00:05:12.268 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The minutes should stay exactly the same.

85
00:05:17.303 --> 00:05:21.963 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Fourteen minus twelve equals two, so
fourteen twenty is two twenty

86
00:05:21.963 --> 00:05:26.673 line:1% position:50% size:90%
in the afternoon. Notice that we did not
subtract twelve from the minutes.

87
00:05:26.673 --> 00:05:29.333 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The twenty minutes remain twenty minutes.

88
00:05:30.321 --> 00:05:32.341 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Be careful around midday.

89
00:05:32.362 --> 00:05:36.131 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Twelve noon is twelve hundred in
twenty-four-hour time.

90
00:05:36.172 --> 00:05:38.352 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Midnight is zero hundred.

91
00:05:38.411 --> 00:05:42.711 line:1% position:50% size:90%
These two moments are twelve hours apart,
even though both may be written as

92
00:05:42.711 --> 00:05:44.831 line:1% position:50% size:90%
twelve on a twelve-hour clock.

93
00:05:45.827 --> 00:05:48.737 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Here is our final independent challenge.

94
00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:53.457 line:1% position:50% size:90%
A train leaves at eleven thirty-five and
reaches its destination at twelve

95
00:05:53.457 --> 00:05:55.767 line:1% position:50% size:90%
twenty. How long does it travel?

96
00:05:55.927 --> 00:06:00.257 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Draw a timeline with noon as the middle
stop and solve each part.

97
00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:09.107 line:1% position:50% size:90%
From eleven thirty-five to noon is
twenty-five minutes.

98
00:06:09.127 --> 00:06:12.577 line:1% position:50% size:90%
From noon to twelve twenty is another
twenty minutes.

99
00:06:12.577 --> 00:06:16.277 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Twenty-five plus twenty equals forty-five
minutes.

100
00:06:16.307 --> 00:06:19.117 line:1% position:50% size:90%
The train journey takes forty-five
minutes.

101
00:06:20.131 --> 00:06:23.921 line:1% position:50% size:90%
To check your understanding, explain the
method to someone else.

102
00:06:23.941 --> 00:06:28.351 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Read the clock hands, choose a helpful
hour boundary, count each jump, and

103
00:06:28.351 --> 00:06:33.111 line:1% position:50% size:90%
add the minutes. If your answer seems
surprising, draw the timeline again.

104
00:06:34.148 --> 00:06:38.588 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Today you read clock hands, crossed an
hour boundary, and converted between

105
00:06:38.588 --> 00:06:41.048 line:1% position:50% size:90%
twelve-hour and twenty-four-hour time.

106
00:06:41.068 --> 00:06:45.158 line:1% position:50% size:90%
Remember: count the time between the two
moments, not just the numbers on

107
00:06:45.158 --> 00:06:45.958 line:1% position:50% size:90%
the clock.
